y delve into and they use the word  unfortunately in relation to the greater  caste because they all have exceptional  designs and personalities that I wanted  to explore so much more than we got to  like you can see their potential so  clearly but due to the medium of film it  just cannot allow for them to truly  shine the way a TV series would and  oddly enough the character I think you  can see this most clearly in is Vinnie  who is the rat mascot of burning rescue  the organization that Gallo and his  posse work for he is adorable in every  scene it he's in and you just know that  if this was a 24 to 27 episode series  that Vinnie would easily become that  iconic mascot in the same fashion as  booter and Gurren Lagann or guts and  kill the kill but while I do think it's  a shame that we didn't get to know the  extended cast that little bit more I  can't do anything but off a wild praise  to the film for creating a world of  people that I did actively want to  become more invested in I mean in a lot  of other productions I can imagine that  these characters would have been heavily  neglected in terms of both design and  performance in order to draw focus to  the primary cast by default but studio  trigger refuses to neglect these  characters in that aspect and I very  much appreciate that and while we're  here almost all of these characters do  take inspiration from previous works as  well so it isn't just scholar gray  Forsyte is another one that immediately  comes to mind because visually let's be  real he is what would have happened if  gamma gory and Ross you had a lovechild  it's just how it is  and I know the main female protagonist  seems very much like a mash-up of Yoko  and ryuko who also happens to pilot her  mech just like zero two from darling in  the Franks references and nods are  everywhere but I can't help but smile  every time I recognize something because  I have such fond memories of all of  these series I mean maybe not so much  darling in the Franks but everything  else in terms of the story this is  easily the weakest element of premiere  the story is it's there it exists and it  does what it sets out to do but it's  nothing special in fact I would be  willing to bet that if you could not  speak Japanese and you watch premiere  without subtitles you'd still be able to  understand the majority of the greater  plot like everything else the story and  its beats ro heavily from previous  titles so much that watching premiere  actually felt like I was watching an  abridged version of a TV series that I  had already seen before like it's not  that I could predict everything that was  about to happen but it all felt  incredibly familiar for the entire  stretch of the film although speaking of  predictability though like I said I  couldn't predict everything but format  is not a film that invests heavily into  the  your plot twists or any sort of  directional shift that you weren't  expecting  for example the characters with the  exception of maybe leo are all very  standard but I don't mean that in a bad  way it's more that as soon as the  character was introduced I knew exactly  what their purpose in the story was  going to be which may potentially remove  something nice for the journey we're  about to go on because I always prefer  not to know the destination but that's  just what it was and it doesn't  necessarily really matter because even  knowing all of that Vermeer is still  incredibly enjoyable due to all of the  work put into every other aspect of the  film they have to say that a lot of that  work went into action because oh boy  this film can get pretty insane during  its action sequences and legitimately  don't think I've ever seen action with  more attention to detail placed into it  than what is on display and premiere  every time someone or something kicked  into gear I knew I was in for some sort  of visual feast although what I will say  is that at times it was possible for it  to be in a bit too much like a lot of  the time the background and foreground  can blend very easily due to the  overwhelming use of vibrant color in  both of them and when this gets applied  to fast-moving sequences there are times  when all I saw was a blur of  incomprehensible stuff right in front of  me however in all fairness I should also  say that I had a splitting headache when  I saw premiere so that may have had  something to do with it the thing is  that even if I wasn't able to visually  consistently place everything that was  going on it still had me very much on  board and it actually made me want to  watch it again to properly appreciate it  there's a lot of master artistry to love  and premiere and I guess that might be  what my action complaint is there's too  much artistry to possibly appreciate it  all in a single viewing which you know  on the spectrum of problems I think is a  pretty good problem to have  far better than having a film which is  completely lacking and a slow to get  through at no point during premiere was  I ever tired of what was happening even  with the headache you know that's just  the result of shifting your efforts to  the realm of visualization in cinema  because you can have the greatest story  ever written with the most wonderful  characters ever performed but it's all  for nothing if you can't convey it  visually which is what films are visual  media and I feel like a lot of projects  may or they enough come to forget that  but as a result it is possible to go  balls to the wall with ascetics based on  a bare-bones story and archetypal  characters and still have it be an  incredible experience I would highly  recommend permit to anybody not just  trigger fans and definitely not just  anime fans I mean yes the high energy  won't be everybody's loaf of bread  especially if you're gluten intolerant  but I think the premiere actually  axé is a very solid ambassador for anime  it's a very good short condensed gateway  experience if you have friends or family  that you'd like to introduce into this  world and you know what even if you  don't go and see it anyway on the big  screen if possible because I suspect the  premiere might lose a lot of its full-on  force on smaller screens plus amazingly  enough it's a film that makes decent use  of CGI I didn't mention that before but  the use of 3d modeling even in anime  films is often fairly cringe and  unnecessary to me  it doesn't generally add anything but  with the geometric focus of premiere it  contributes significantly to the feel of  the world so no worries there but yeah I  loved premiere not as much as Gran logon  or kill the kill and there was nothing  earth-shattering but it was a highly  enjoyable experience provided by a  pretty phenomenal production company and  as always I'm keenly awaiting the next  project but that pretty much does it for  this non-spoiler review of premiere if  you enjoyed this video and the content  this channel produced in general then  please do consider donating to the new  world to view patreon because the  support of all the amazing people is  what continues to make this channel  possible and if patreon isn't quite your  style then please do leave this video  will like share or subscribe because it  also helps for this channel an  incredible amount and if you'd like to  join the fun at any time and please do  head over to my discord server where a  wide array of shenanigan tree takes  place on a daily basis and finally  please do comment with your thoughts  from n this has been the new world  review and I'll see you next time  you

